            <ArticleTitle>Acute rupture of an aortic aneurysm mimicking the discus hernia syndrome. A case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>142-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Aneurysms of the abdominal aorta have been recognised as a cause of back pain and vertebral erosion. However back pain and paraplegia are uncommon, presenting complaints in patients with aortic aneurysms. A case of acute rupture of an abdominal aortic aneurysm is presented mimicking the symptoms of a discus hernia syndrome and paraplegia.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
